# MagSafe Guard (sutz2001 fork)

> **Keep in sync with:** `.github/copilot-instructions.md` and `AGENTS.md`  
> Update **both** Cursor and Copilot instruction files in the same commit when conventions change.

## README (required)

- **English:** `README.md` (primary)
- **German:** `README.de.md` (must stay in sync)
- Cross-link at the top of both files
- When changing features, defaults, actions, build steps, or fork-specific settings → update **both** READMEs in the same PR/commit
- Remove stale Taskmaster export blocks from README; use tables in README for feature status instead

## Fork identity

- Remote fork: `sutz2001/MagSafe-BusKill`
- Upstream: `lekman/magsafe-buskill` (remote `upstream`)
- Bundle ID: `com.sutz2001.MagSafeGuard` — never restore `com.LekmanConsulting.*` or team `PW6K4BERFV`
- Personal Team: no iCloud/Push in `MagSafeGuard/MagSafeGuard.entitlements`

## Defaults (document in README when changed)

- Grace period: **30 s** (range 5–30 s) — `SettingsModel.gracePeriodDuration`
- Default security actions: lock screen + sound alarm
- Config static members: `.defaultConfig` (not `.default`)

## Version bump checklist

1. `MagSafeGuard.xcodeproj` → `MARKETING_VERSION` and `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION`
2. `docs/CHANGELOG.md` entry
3. Git tag `vX.Y.Z` on release
4. Both README files if user-visible behavior changed
5. `.github/copilot-instructions.md` if agent/convention rules changed

## Build commands (prefer Taskfile)

```bash
task setup && task build && task test
open MagSafeGuard.xcodeproj   # ⌘R in Xcode
```

Do not use raw `swift test` / `xcodebuild` when `task` equivalents exist.

## Security actions (only these five)

`lockScreen`, `soundAlarm`, `forceLogout`, `shutdown`, `customScript` — document in README; do not claim unmount/wipe without implementation.

## Safety

- Real system actions when armed — do not run/build the app without user intent
- No secrets in commits; blocked commit words: `claude`, `anthropic`, `co-authored`
